[{:adr/authoritative_for ["mangaka.layout.komawari's `styles` map (:toriyama {:tilt-enabled? true :frame-break? false}, :togashi {:tilt-enabled? false :frame-break? true}) gates BOTH row-tilt and :beat/inset -- a beat's :beat/inset is a no-op under any style with :frame-break? false" "the :togashi geometry preset is evidence-grounded, not a guess: analysis of two real Hunter x Hunter (Yoshihiro Togashi, Succession War arc) reference pages found ZERO force-line diagonal panel shearing -- panels stay rectilinear even in tense confrontations; dynamism instead comes from panel-in-panel overlap (apply-inset), tight-crop framing, and background render-density contrast between adjacent panels" "apply-inset shrinks a beat's rect toward the trailing edge of its cell and grows its height past its own row's band into the row below by :overlap fraction -- the panel-in-panel frame-break device (e.g. a raised-hand interrupt panel overlapping the crowd panel beneath it); the resulting panel is tagged :panel/tags [\"frame-break\"] and validate-layout treats that SPECIFIC overlap as intentional rather than an error" "mangaka.domain gained a :panel/layers component entity mirroring :panel/bubbles/:panel/sfx exactly (schema entry, layer-keys, layer->tx, doc-pull, pulled->panel, valid-panel! structural check, export-lexicon) -- :layer/rect is deliberately NOT bounds-checked at the domain layer (a :layer/bleed character layer legally exceeds its panel's own rect on purpose)" "mangaka.preview draws :panel/layers z-sorted as translucent colored rects over the panel's own white base, with a red dashed stroke on :layer/bleed layers so overflow past the panel border is visible rather than silently clipped" "resources/komawari_styles.edn is scoped to PANEL GEOMETRY + LAYERING only -- it explicitly does not re-derive bubble shape / text weight / dialogue register / background tone, which already exist (also Hunter x Hunter-sourced) in kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-mangaka-expression-clj's resources/mangaka_expression_patterns.edn; the two catalogs cross-reference via :expression-crossref rather than duplicate" "two real bugs were found and fixed only by writing graph-level (not just pure-function) tests: :beat/inset was being applied regardless of style (contradicting the style catalog's :frame-break? flag) until row-tilt-style gating was added to it too; and mangaka.graphs.compose-komawari's plan fn was not threading :style from input through to propose-page-layout at all" "a live demo proved the same beat content (a raised-hand interrupt panel + a crowd-reaction panel) produces genuinely different geometry when composeKomawari is invoked with :style :toriyama (force-line shear) vs :style :togashi (panel-in-panel + layered background/character with bleed) -- both pass the governor with zero issues"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "komawari-artist-styles-and-panel-layering", :adr/related ["adr-2607051520"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607051530-komawari-artist-styles-and-panel-layering", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-06", :adr/body "See the companion .md file in this same directory for the full context, decision, consequences, and alternatives (identical content, kept in sync).", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/artifacts "{:ai-gftd-mangaka \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka @ 885a03ef2e86f421a920511e278a38cbc49fc9ff (PR #4, merged -- same commit as ADR-2607051520, both landed in one PR) -- styles/style-opts/apply-inset added to layout/komawari.cljc; :panel/layers component added to domain.cljc; layer-svg rendering added to preview.cljc; compose_komawari.cljc :style passthrough bug fixed; resources/komawari_styles.edn (new); clojure -M:dev:test 93 tests/577 assertions, 1 failure/1 error both pre-existing (comfy-stub env, unrelated -- same two as ADR-2607051520's baseline)\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-05", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607051530: komawari artist-style catalog(toriyama/togashi)+ panel layering", :adr/source-format "edn"}]